## SUMMARY

Architecture locks for router catalog, Authorizer trust path, I→A→V order, K/L fail-closed, RFL hard-cut, migration sextuple, and host scope are coherent and prior Low/Medium fixes hold. **NEEDS_FIXES** on three implementer-facing gaps: ordinary SM does not mirror locked V two-clean the way I/A do; leaf-Step A-loop exception lacks a receipt rule; V two-clean lacks a named traceability owner while I/A/K-L do. Clarify remains a thin routing brief relative to Iterate/migration/SM depth the plan already locks — one short Q12–Q20 (or “locks by reference”) pass closes the parity hole without reopening settled Q1–Q11.
